
  <sn><md>### Salt Movement in Soil

**Definition:**
Salt movement in soil refers to the **transport, accumulation, and redistribution of soluble salts** (Na⁺, Ca²⁺, Mg²⁺, Cl⁻, SO₄²⁻, CO₃²⁻, HCO₃⁻) within the soil profile. It is driven mainly by **water movement** and **evaporation**.

![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-emon/QDoc/main/SES3/Soil%20and%20Enviromental%20Chemistry/05.Liquid%20Phase/assets/soil_movement_diagram.jpeg)

</md></sn>
